\begin{slide}
\slidetitle{Introduction}
Hello and welcome to this presentation about \em{VernierOffice}, an
experimental semantic document language.

Key points:
\begin{itemize}
\item Separate content from presentation
\item Write once, compile to multiple formats
\item Semantic markup with \code{\\em\{text\}}
\end{itemize}
\end{slide}

\begin{slide}
\slidetitle{Text Formatting}
This slide demonstrates inline formatting:

\begin{itemize}
\item \em{Emphasis} level 1 — italic
\item \em{2}{Strong emphasis} level 2 — bold
\item \em{3}{Very strong} level 3 — bold italic
\end{itemize}

Chemical formulas: H\sub{2}O. Mathematics: E = mc\super{2}.
Inline code: \code{let x = 42;}.
\end{slide}

\begin{slide}
\slidetitle{Tables and Data}
